What Was Implemented


shelter.fxml
Added addressField (TextField) — labelled "Address", prompt text "e.g. Meppadi, Wayanad, Kerala 673577" — positioned above the coordinates section
Regrouped lat/lng fields into a side-by-side HBox under label "Coordinates (optional)"
Added btnAutoFill (Button with styleClass="btn-geocode") — "📍 Auto-fill coordinates from address" — with a Tooltip explaining Nominatim and offline fallback
Renamed the table column from "Coordinates" → "Address" (fx:id="colAddress")
Added <?import javafx.scene.control.Tooltip?> import


ShelterController.java
ShelterRow: added address field; constructor updated; getAddress() getter added; coordinates is now internal-only (used in formatCoordinates() for tooltip-level tracking)
@FXML bindings: addressField, btnAutoFill wired; colAddress replaces colCoordinates; colAddress binds to getAddress() so the table shows text, not raw lat/lng
handleAutoFillCoordinates(): uses Java 11 HttpClient (no extra dependency) to call Nominatim; button shows "⏳ Looking up..." while in-flight; on success populates lat/lng fields to 6dp; on network failure shows a graceful offline message
handleFind(): now also populates addressField from the found row
handleClear(): clears addressField
applyRoleRestrictions(): hides btnAutoFill for non-admin roles (along with the other write controls)


application.css
Added Section 15 — .btn-geocode with teal dashed border (visually distinct from primary/success buttons — communicates "optional helper"), hover state, and a :disabled state for the in-flight loading phase